    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"org_chart - EdgeCase\", \"isPartOf\": {\"@type\":\n    \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/org_chart.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [org_chart()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label .doc-label-function}\n    | EdgeCase\n  description: A company's reporting lines.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [org_chart()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label .doc-label-function}\n    | EdgeCase\n  description: A company's reporting lines.\ntitle: >-\n  [org_chart()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label .doc-label-function}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: A company's reporting lines.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nA company's reporting lines.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/example_networks.py#L2016-L2104){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\norg_chart()\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\nThe organization chart of a made-up company of 20 people, with an edge from each manager\nto each person who reports to them. Everyone but the chief executive has exactly one\nmanager, so the graph is a rooted tree (an arborescence). It's the example for trees and\nhierarchies: depth, ancestors and descendants, the lowest common ancestor of two people\n(the most junior manager they share), and drawing a tree top-down.\n\nNetwork Properties:\n\n- 20 nodes (people, labeled by first name)\n- 19 edges (from manager to report)\n- Directed, acyclic, unweighted\n- An arborescence rooted at the chief executive, Mira\n\nNode Attributes:\n\n- `title`: the person's job title, such as `\"Tech Lead\"`\n- `dept`: the department, `\"Executive\"`, `\"Engineering\"`, `\"Finance\"`, `\"Sales\"` or\n  `\"People\"`\n- `level`: how many levels below the chief executive the person is, from `0` to `6`\n- `pos`: an `(x, y)` position for drawing the chart top-down, with each manager centered\n  over their reports\n\nWhat to Look For:\n\n- **A deep chain.** Engineering has six levels below the chief executive, down to the\n  intern Noor, while Sales has one: `dag_longest_path()` runs from Mira to Noor.\n- **A wide team.** Sam, the sales director, has 6 direct reports, more than anyone else.\n- **Lowest common ancestors.** The most junior manager Noor and Pia share is Ruth, and\n  for Noor and Ada, in another department, it's Mira.\n- **The top isn't the middle.** In the undirected view, the people the fewest steps from\n  everyone are Jonas and Ines, partway down the long engineering chain, not Mira. Mira\n  does have the highest betweenness, since every path between departments goes through\n  the chief executive.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [Graph]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   The organization chart.\n:::\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nDraw the chart top-down, colored by department:\n\n::: {#d1e4bae1 .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\norg = ec.org_chart()\n\norg.plot(layout=\"pos\", color_by=\"dept\", label_by=\"label\", height=420)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}}:is(html.quarto-light, body.quarto-light, html[data-bs-theme=\"light\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"true\"], body.vscode-light, body.vscode-high-contrast-light, html[theme=\"light\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}:is(html.quarto-dark, body.quarto-dark, html[data-bs-theme=\"dark\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"false\"], body.vscode-dark, body.vscode-high-contrast:not(.vscode-high-contrast-light), html[theme=\"dark\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}</style><div class=\"ec-plot\" style=\"position:relative;width:fit-content;max-width:100%;margin:1em auto\">\n<style>.ec-plot > svg { display:block; max-width:100%; height:auto; }</style>\n<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"700\" height=\"420\" viewBox=\"52.5 6.5 711.6 427.0\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif;\">\n<rect x=\"52.5\" y=\"6.5\" width=\"711.6\" height=\"427.0\" fill=\"var(--ect-3239c383)\"/>\n<g opacity=\"0.4\"><line x1=\"250.0\" y1=\"126.0\" x2=\"250.0\" y2=\"132.0\" stroke=\"#e15759\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><polygon p